   "problem": "Two misstatements. (1) 'ainda que seja aquilo que se esperava' reads as a claim that the question WAS expected, which is the opposite of 予期していなかった; the point being made is that その質問 is what the verb takes as its object yet surfaces as topic. (2) 'nao era algo que ELE vinha esperando' invents a third-person subject: the subject is unstated and, in a plain past statement like this, defaults to the speaker.",
